WEBVTT

00:00:07.382 --> 00:00:09.384
♪ ♪

00:00:14.305 --> 00:00:17.266
( cameras clicking )

00:00:21.896 --> 00:00:24.399
( crunching )

00:00:26.109 --> 00:00:29.570
( smacking )

00:00:34.283 --> 00:00:37.078
( cameras clicking )

00:00:40.748 --> 00:00:43.251
Daddy, I want to go in.

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:45.586
It’s 9:59, sweetheart.

00:00:45.628 --> 00:00:47.922
Make time go faster.

00:00:48.006 --> 00:00:50.049
Do you think Mr. Wonka
will recognize you?

00:00:50.091 --> 00:00:51.592
Hard to say.

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:53.261
It’s been years.

00:00:53.302 --> 00:00:55.638
( crunching )

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:02.937
Eyes on the prize, Violet.

00:01:02.979 --> 00:01:05.273
Eyes on the prize.

00:01:11.195 --> 00:01:13.406
( clanking, squeaking )

00:01:13.448 --> 00:01:16.242
( excited murmuring )

00:01:17.285 --> 00:01:18.661
( cameras clicking )

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:26.586
WONKA ( over speaker ):
Please enter.

00:01:37.138 --> 00:01:41.142
Come... forward.

00:01:43.686 --> 00:01:46.314
( over speaker ):
Close the gates.

00:01:46.355 --> 00:01:49.150
( creaking, squeaking )

00:01:52.904 --> 00:01:54.030
( creaking )

00:01:54.113 --> 00:01:55.656
( loud clank )

00:01:55.698 --> 00:01:58.034
( over speaker ):
Dear visitors,

00:01:58.117 --> 00:02:00.036
it is my great pleasure
to welcome you

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:01.704
to my humble factory.

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:04.165
( pipe organ plays
dramatic tune )

00:02:04.248 --> 00:02:06.667
( over speaker ):
And who am I?

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:10.546
Well...

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:13.007
( sprightly music plays )

00:02:13.049 --> 00:02:14.842
♪ Hee-hee, ha-ha, ho-ho, ho-ho ♪

00:02:14.884 --> 00:02:16.511
♪ Willy Wonka, Willy Wonka ♪

00:02:16.594 --> 00:02:18.805
♪ The amazing chocolatier!
Whee! ♪

00:02:18.846 --> 00:02:20.681
♪ Willy Wonka, Willy Wonka ♪

00:02:20.765 --> 00:02:22.433
♪ Everybody give a cheer,
hooray! ♪

00:02:22.517 --> 00:02:25.019
♪ He’s modest, clever
and so smart ♪

00:02:25.061 --> 00:02:26.729
♪ He barely can restrain it ♪

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:30.775
♪ With so much generosity, there
is no way to contain it! Whee! ♪

00:02:30.858 --> 00:02:34.403
♪ To contain it, to contain,
to contain, to contain ♪

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.572
♪ Ha-ha, hee-hee, ho-ho,
hooray! Ha-ha! Whee! ♪

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:38.199
♪ Willy Wonka, Willy Wonka ♪

00:02:38.282 --> 00:02:40.368
♪ He’s the one that children
flock to meet ♪

00:02:40.409 --> 00:02:42.578
♪ Willy Wonka, Willy Wonka ♪

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:44.539
♪ He’s a genius
who just can’t be beat ♪

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:47.125
♪ A magician
and a chocolate whiz ♪

00:02:47.208 --> 00:02:49.043
♪ The best darn guy
who ever lived ♪

00:02:49.085 --> 00:02:54.924
♪ Willy Wonka, here he is! ♪

00:02:55.007 --> 00:02:56.968
( melody continues )

00:02:57.051 --> 00:02:58.845
( whizzing, popping )

00:03:03.808 --> 00:03:05.518
( groans, sputters )

00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:10.731
( music slowing down )

00:03:13.276 --> 00:03:17.822
♪ The amazing chocolatier...
Whee... ♪

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:26.414
( manic giggling )

00:03:26.455 --> 00:03:28.124
Wasn’t that just
magnificent?

00:03:28.207 --> 00:03:30.459
I was worried it was
getting a little dodgy

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:33.921
in the middle part,
but then that finale-- wow!

00:03:37.216 --> 00:03:38.467
Who are you?

00:03:40.052 --> 00:03:42.013
He’s Willy Wonka.

00:03:42.096 --> 00:03:43.306
Really?

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:55.193
Good morning, Starshine.

00:03:55.276 --> 00:03:57.778
The Earth says hello.

00:03:57.862 --> 00:04:00.281
( fire crackling )

00:04:05.828 --> 00:04:08.956
"Dear guests, greetings.

00:04:08.998 --> 00:04:10.333
"Welcome to the factory.

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:13.211
I shake you warmly by the hand."

00:04:14.462 --> 00:04:16.297
( glove squeaks )

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:18.466
"My name is Willy Wonka."

00:04:18.507 --> 00:04:19.592
( giggles )

00:04:19.634 --> 00:04:21.135
Then shouldn’t you be up there?

00:04:21.219 --> 00:04:24.472
Well, I couldn’t very well
watch the show from up there,

00:04:24.513 --> 00:04:25.806
now, could I, little girl?

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:27.642
Mr. Wonka,

00:04:27.683 --> 00:04:29.644
I don’t know
if you remember me,

00:04:29.727 --> 00:04:32.688
but I used to work
here in the factory.

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:35.024
Were you one of those
despicable spies

00:04:35.107 --> 00:04:36.275
who every day tried to steal

00:04:36.317 --> 00:04:37.610
my life’s work
and sell it

00:04:37.652 --> 00:04:40.488
to those parasitic
copycat candy-making cads?

00:04:40.571 --> 00:04:41.656
No, sir.

00:04:41.697 --> 00:04:43.991
Then wonderful.
Welcome back.

00:04:44.075 --> 00:04:45.826
Let’s get a move on, kids.

00:04:47.828 --> 00:04:50.665
Don’t you want to know
our names?

00:04:50.748 --> 00:04:52.541
Can’t imagine
how it would matter.

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:53.793
( large door rumbles )

00:04:53.834 --> 00:04:56.295
Come quickly.
Far too much to see.

00:04:59.298 --> 00:05:00.299
( loud clank )

00:05:00.341 --> 00:05:03.678
Just drop your coats anywhere.

00:05:09.308 --> 00:05:12.687
Mr. Wonka,
sure is toasty in here.

00:05:12.728 --> 00:05:13.896
What?! Oh, yeah.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:16.023
I have to keep it warm in here
because my workers

00:05:16.065 --> 00:05:17.233
are used
to an extremely

00:05:17.316 --> 00:05:18.317
hot climate.

00:05:18.359 --> 00:05:20.319
They just can’t stand the cold.

00:05:20.361 --> 00:05:21.612
Who are the workers?

00:05:22.446 --> 00:05:23.656
WONKA:
All in good time.

00:05:23.698 --> 00:05:24.740
Now...

00:05:27.868 --> 00:05:28.744
( gasps )

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:30.871
Mr. Wonka,
I’m Violet Beauregarde.

00:05:30.955 --> 00:05:32.498
Oh.

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:33.708
( smacking )

00:05:33.791 --> 00:05:34.834
I don’t care.

00:05:34.875 --> 00:05:36.419
Well, you should care,
because I’m the girl

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:38.462
who’s going to win
the special prize at the end.

00:05:38.546 --> 00:05:40.923
Well, you do seem confident,
and confidence is key.

00:05:44.135 --> 00:05:45.011
I’m Veruca Salt.

00:05:45.052 --> 00:05:46.095
( gasps )

00:05:46.178 --> 00:05:47.722
It’s very nice to meet you, sir.

00:05:47.763 --> 00:05:50.433
I always thought a veruca
was a type of wart

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:51.767
you got on the
bottom of your foot.

00:05:51.851 --> 00:05:54.228
( laughs )

00:05:54.312 --> 00:05:56.147
( muffled ):
I’m Augustus Gloop.

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:57.857
I love your chocolate.

00:05:58.816 --> 00:06:00.026
I can see that.

00:06:00.067 --> 00:06:01.402
So do I.

00:06:01.444 --> 00:06:04.989
I never expected to have
so much in common.

00:06:08.826 --> 00:06:09.952
You.

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:11.662
You’re Mike Teavee.

00:06:11.746 --> 00:06:14.582
You’re the little devil
who cracked the system.

00:06:16.042 --> 00:06:17.251
And you.

00:06:17.293 --> 00:06:19.754
Well, you’re just lucky
to be here, aren’t you?

00:06:21.297 --> 00:06:24.925
And the rest of you
must be their p...

00:06:31.807 --> 00:06:32.767
Parents.

00:06:32.808 --> 00:06:34.101
Yeah.

00:06:34.185 --> 00:06:37.646
Moms and dads.

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:40.107
Dad?

00:06:41.108 --> 00:06:43.611
Papa?

00:06:49.617 --> 00:06:52.787
Okay, then. Let’s move along.

00:07:02.505 --> 00:07:03.672
Would you like
some chocolate?

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:04.632
Sure.

00:07:04.673 --> 00:07:06.759
Then you should’ve
brought some.

00:07:10.054 --> 00:07:11.514
Let’s be friends.

00:07:11.597 --> 00:07:12.848
Best friends.

